:name: RA4M1 HAL serial-bus smoke (SCI UART / RIIC I2C / RSPI SPI)
:description: Boots a real ra4m1-hal serial-bus example ELF on the UNO R4 Minima
:             platform, adding the stock SCI/IIC wiring the drivers need plus a
:             custom SPI model and a mock I2C slave.
:
: Run headless from the REPO ROOT (paths are repo-relative; Renode's monitor
: cannot tokenize the spaces/parens some checkout paths contain, so keep the
: working directory at the repo root and use relative @paths):
:
:   cd <repo-root>
:   <renode-install>/renode --console --disable-xwt --plain \
:     -e '$elf=@target/thumbv7em-none-eabihf/release/examples/spi' \
:     -e 'include @renode/serial.resc' \
:     -e 'start'
:
: Swap $elf to .../examples/uart or .../examples/i2c for the other buses.
: The automated pass/fail lives in renode/serial.robot (run via renode-test).

$elf ?= @target/thumbv7em-none-eabihf/release/examples/spi

# Compile the custom models (adds Timers.Ra4m1Gpt320, SPI.Ra4m1Spi,
# I2C.MockI2CSlave) BEFORE the platform description references them.
include @renode/Ra4m1Gpt320.cs
include @renode/Ra4m1Spi.cs
include @renode/MockI2CSlave.cs

mach create "uno-r4-serial"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @renode/ra4m1-uno-r4.repl

# Serial-bus fragment layered on the base platform (see renode/serial.robot for
# the divergence notes this encodes):
#   - sci2: re-point the SCI2 RXI/TXI/TEI to the ICU events the HAL driver
#     programs (sci.rs Sci2: 0x97/0x98/0x99).  The stock repl wires SCI2 to
#     0xA3/0xA4/0xA5 instead; the register LAYOUT matches, only the event
#     numbers diverge (both are FSP assumptions — BENCH-VERIFY).  Without this
#     the async echo's RXI never reaches IEL2 and the echo stalls.
#   - spi0: bind the custom RSPI model over the stock SPI0 Tag @ 0x40072000,
#     wiring SPRI/SPTI to the driver-assumed events (spi.rs Spi0: 0xA1/0xA2).
#   - mockSlave: a register-file I2C slave at address 0x50 on iic0.  (iic0's
#     stock IRQ wiring 0x035..0x038 already MATCHES i2c.rs — no rewire needed.)
machine LoadPlatformDescriptionFromString
"""
sci2:
    ReceiveIRQ -> icu@0x97
    TransmitIRQ -> icu@0x98
    TransmitEndIRQ -> icu@0x99

spi0: SPI.Ra4m1Spi @ sysbus 0x40072000
    ReceiveIRQ -> icu@0xA1
    TransmitIRQ -> icu@0xA2

mockSlave: I2C.MockI2CSlave @ iic0 0x50
"""

sysbus LoadELF $elf

# This script only builds the machine; issue `start` (or `emulation RunFor`)
# after including it so the caller controls a deterministic, bounded run.
#   uart: Create Terminal Tester sysbus.sci2; Write/Wait For Line (echo)
#   spi:  sysbus.spi0 TransferCount / FirstByte / LastRxByte
#   i2c:  sysbus.iic0.mockSlave TransactionCount
